; getline_short_stack_int_register: GETLINE pops its index before it reads
; its register, so an empty stack raises StackUnderflow even though the
; register would also have been rejected.
;
; spec/xqvm/SPEC.md's error-precedence rule makes operand pops first within
; every instruction. Twenty-two runners in xqvm_py resolved the register
; first, so programs of this shape raised TYPE_MISMATCH there and
; STACK_UNDERFLOW on the Rust VM. Both VMs rejected them, but the Faults
; table makes the identity normative, so two names for one program is a
; divergence.
;
; GETLINE stands for the whole family here; xqvm_py's own suite covers all
; twenty-two off the opcode table. The register is filled from calldata
; rather than left unset for the reason iter_short_stack_int_register gives:
; an unset register would raise UNSET_REGISTER on both VMs and would not
; discriminate the order.

PUSH 0
INPUT r0         ; r0 = 5, an int
GETLINE r0       ; nothing on the stack for it to pop
HALT
